def LAD(*a): return list(a)
def RUB(a,b,c,d): return [(a,'Missing or unclear','Meets the stated check',b),(c,'Guessing','Evidence kept',d),('Records','Gaps','Complete','Complete and reviewed by a peer'),('Safety and ethics','Overlooked','Followed','Followed and taught to others')]
COURSES = [
dict(slug='vacations-and-rentals', title='Vacations and Rentals Operations', level='L4 Practitioner',
 summary='Plan and run holiday stays and rentals with fair pricing, clean and safe spaces, clear guest information and honest records, so that guests return and the property earns more than it costs.',
 outs=[('Define','guest types, seasons and local rental rules.'),('Apply','a booking, check-in and cleaning routine.'),('Analyse','occupancy, average daily rate and profit.'),('Evaluate','safety, legal and review risks.'),('Create','a guest guide, a price plan and a yearly calendar.')],
 task='Prepare a rental for guests and run one full booking cycle from enquiry to check-out with a price plan and complete records.', cond='About 8 weeks part-time. A real or model property with at least two rooms, a booking sheet, a cleaning checklist, a mentor.',
 standard='The property passes a 30-point safety and cleanliness check, every booking has a written confirmation and receipt, and income, costs and occupancy are recorded and reconciled for the month.', who='Property owners, homestay and villa hosts, tourism and hospitality students.', req='None.',
 mods=[
 M('Know your guests and the rules','Define',4,['Group guests into families, couples, solo travellers, friend groups and work travellers, and list what each needs.','List seasons in your area: peak, shoulder and low, with school-holiday and festival dates.','Find the local rules: registration with the local tourism office, police guest records, fire safety, tax on room rent and any society or panchayat rules.','Collect guest ID as the law requires and store it safely.'],'A hill-town homestay has two rooms. Families book in May and June, couples in October to December. Rules checked: guest register kept for each stay, ID copy stored in a locked drawer, tax registration needed once yearly room sales pass the legal limit.','Write profiles for three guest types and a one-page rule checklist for your area.','Each profile lists at least four needs, and the checklist names at least five rules with the office that governs each.','Why keep a guest register?','The law requires it and it helps in an emergency.'),
 M('Prepare a safe and clean space','Apply',6,['Walk the property with a 30-point checklist: locks, lights, water, power, stairs, balcony rails, mattresses, bathrooms, kitchen.','Keep a first aid box, fire extinguisher, torch and a list of local emergency numbers in view.','Check gas cylinder, regulator, geyser and wiring for faults before every season, and switch off the gas at the cylinder when not in use.','Clean in order: top to bottom, dry to wet, and change all linen between guests.'],'Checklist score 27 of 30. Three faults: loose balcony rail, no night light on stairs, geyser earth wire missing. All fixed within two days at a cost of Rs 1,850 before the first booking.','Inspect a property with the checklist and fix or report every fault.','Score is at least 28 of 30 and every fault has a dated action.','Which is cleaned first, floor or ceiling fan?','The ceiling fan, because dust falls down.'),
 M('Furnish and stock for comfort','Apply',5,['List the basics per room: bed, two pillows, two sets of sheets, towels, curtains, hooks, a bin with a lid.','Stock the kitchen to match the guest type: kettle, pans, plates for the group size, drinking water filter.','Keep a consumables list: soap, toilet paper, cleaning liquid, tea, sugar, cooking gas.','Count stock after each stay and record losses and breakage.'],'For a family of five a two-room unit needs 6 plates, 6 glasses, 2 towels per person and 2 sheet sets per bed. Annual breakage cost on average is Rs 3,000, so a breakage line is added to costs.','Build a stock list and an inventory sheet for one unit.','List covers every room and a count is done after one stay.','Why count stock after every stay?','To find losses early and restock before the next guest.'),
 M('Set prices that fit','Create',6,['Work out cost per night: share of loan or rent, electricity, water, staff, cleaning, repairs and platform fees.','Check what three similar places nearby charge in each season.','Set a base rate, then a peak rate, a low rate and a weekly discount.','Add extra charges clearly: extra bed, extra guest, cooking gas, firewood.'],'Monthly fixed cost Rs 18,000 plus variable Rs 400 per stay. Expected 15 nights a month means break-even is Rs 1,200 plus Rs 400 per stay, so base rate is set at Rs 2,200 and peak at Rs 3,000.','Build a price table for three seasons with a break-even calculation.','Every rate is above break-even and the table is compared to three nearby places.','What is break-even rate?','The lowest price at which income equals cost.'),
 M('Take bookings and communicate','Apply',5,['Reply to every enquiry within two hours with dates, price, rules and what is included.','Take an advance, for example 30 percent, and send a written confirmation with a booking number.','Use a booking calendar so one night is never sold twice, and block repair days.','Send directions, check-in time and a contact number two days before arrival.'],'Enquiry for 4 nights at Rs 2,200: total Rs 8,800, advance Rs 2,640 received, balance Rs 6,160 at check-in, confirmation number B-014, cancellation rule stated in writing.','Run five mock bookings and fill in the calendar and confirmation messages.','No double bookings, each confirmation shows price, advance, balance and rule.','Why send a written confirmation?','It avoids disputes about price and dates.'),
 M('Run check-in, stay and check-out','Apply',5,['Greet the guest, collect ID, show the rooms and explain water, power, gas and house rules.','Give a printed guest guide with the emergency numbers, nearest hospital and Wi-Fi details.','Check the room with the guest at check-out and note damage on the same day.','Return any deposit within a stated time, with reasons for deductions.'],'A guest breaks a glass worth Rs 150 and leaves a Rs 1,000 deposit. At check-out Rs 850 is returned with a receipt listing the deduction.','Role-play a check-in and a check-out with a peer.','Peer confirms every item on the check-in list was covered.','What is the purpose of a deposit?','To cover damage and make guests careful.'),
 M('Track income, costs and reviews','Analyse',6,['Record each stay: nights, rate, income, platform fee and cleaning cost.','Work out occupancy: nights sold divided by nights available.','Work out average daily rate: income divided by nights sold.','Read reviews monthly, group complaints by cause and fix the top one.'],'In a 30-day month 18 nights sold gives 60 percent occupancy. Income Rs 40,500 gives an average daily rate of Rs 2,250. Costs Rs 24,000 leave a profit of Rs 16,500. Two reviews mention weak Wi-Fi, so the router is upgraded.','Prepare a one-month report with occupancy, average daily rate and profit.','Figures reconcile to the booking sheet and at least one action follows from reviews.','How do you calculate occupancy?','Nights sold divided by nights available.'),
 M('Capstone: a full booking cycle','Create',5,['Prepare the property and pass the 30-point check.','Publish the price table and take a booking from enquiry to check-out.','Write the guest guide and a risk list with actions.','Present the month report and a plan for the next season.'],'One property, one 3-night stay, income Rs 6,600, costs Rs 1,900, a guest guide of two pages and a risk list of eight items.','Present the whole cycle to a mentor.','All records tie out and the mentor signs the safety check.','What proves the cycle worked?','Complete records, a safe property and a profitable stay.')],
 extra=[('What should a rental do if a guest falls ill at night?','Call the emergency number or nearest hospital, help calmly and record what happened.'),('Why list rules in the guest guide?','Clear rules prevent damage, noise complaints and disputes.')],
 rubric=RUB('Safety and cleanliness','Checklist passed and faults fixed with dates','Pricing','Based on cost, season and nearby rates'),
 ladder=LAD('Know guest needs.','Clean and prepare a space safely.','Take bookings and run a stay.','Run a property for a season with records.','Manage several properties and staff.','Lead a rental business with quality standards.','Shape local tourism standards and training.'),
 jobs=['Homestay host','Rental manager','Guest relations executive','Property caretaker','Reservations coordinator']),

dict(slug='bookkeeping-and-accounting', title='Bookkeeping and Accounting for Small Businesses', level='L4 Practitioner',
 summary='Record transactions, reconcile bank and cash, prepare basic statements and meet tax and audit needs for a small business, with entries that balance and evidence that is kept.',
 outs=[('Define','assets, liabilities, equity, income and expense.'),('Apply','double entry to everyday transactions.'),('Analyse','a trial balance and find errors.'),('Evaluate','controls, tax obligations and risks of fraud.'),('Create','monthly statements and a filing calendar.')],
 task='Keep the books of a small business for one month, reconcile the bank, and produce a trial balance, profit and loss and balance sheet.', cond='About 10 weeks part-time. A spreadsheet or free accounting tool, 40 sample invoices and receipts, a bank statement, a mentor.',
 standard='Every entry has a source document and balances, the bank reconciles to zero difference, and the balance sheet agrees with the trial balance.', who='Bookkeepers, shop owners, commerce students, office assistants.', req='Basic arithmetic.',
 mods=[
 M('Accounts and the equation','Define',4,['State the equation: assets equal liabilities plus equity.','Group accounts into assets, liabilities, equity, income and expense.','Debit increases assets and expenses; credit increases liabilities, equity and income.','Build a chart of accounts with codes, for example 1000 for assets and 4000 for income.'],'A trader starts with Rs 1,00,000 cash from the owner and buys stock for Rs 40,000 in cash. Cash is Rs 60,000, stock Rs 40,000, equity Rs 1,00,000. Both sides total Rs 1,00,000.','Build a chart of 25 accounts for a shop.','Chart covers all five groups and each account has a code.','State the accounting equation.','Assets equal liabilities plus equity.'),
 M('Record source documents','Apply',5,['Collect invoices, bills, receipts, bank entries and cash vouchers for every transaction.','Check each bill for date, name, amount, tax number and tax amount.','Number and file documents in date order, paper or scanned.','Keep records for the years the law requires.'],'A purchase bill for Rs 11,800 shows Rs 10,000 goods plus Rs 1,800 tax at 18 percent. A bill without a tax number is flagged and the supplier is asked for a corrected copy.','Sort and check 40 documents, flagging the faulty ones.','All documents are numbered and every fault is recorded.','Why must each entry have a document?','It proves the transaction for audit and tax.'),
 M('Journal entries','Apply',6,['Write the date, accounts, debit, credit, amount and a short narration.','Record a cash sale: debit cash, credit sales.','Record a credit purchase: debit purchases and input tax, credit supplier.','Record the payment of expenses such as rent and wages with evidence.'],'Sale Rs 5,000 cash: debit cash Rs 5,000, credit sales Rs 5,000. Rent paid Rs 8,000: debit rent Rs 8,000, credit bank Rs 8,000.','Record 30 entries from the documents.','Total debits equal total credits in every entry.','What is a narration?','A short note explaining the entry.'),
 M('Ledger and trial balance','Analyse',6,['Post each entry to its ledger account and find the balance of each account.','List all balances in a trial balance with debit and credit columns.','If the totals differ, check the difference for a missing posting or a flipped entry.','Divide the difference by nine to see if two digits were swapped.'],'Trial balance debits Rs 4,38,200 and credits Rs 4,38,020. Difference Rs 180 is divisible by nine, so a swap such as 240 posted as 420 on the debit side is found in the wages account.','Prepare a trial balance and trace one planted error.','Totals agree and the error is corrected with a dated entry.','What does a trial balance prove?','That total debits equal total credits.'),
 M('Bank and cash reconciliation','Analyse',5,['Match each bank line to the cash book entry.','List cheques issued but not cleared and deposits not yet credited.','Record bank charges and interest found only in the statement.','Count physical cash and compare with the book balance.'],'Cash book Rs 92,400 less charges Rs 300 gives Rs 92,100. Bank statement Rs 97,600 less unpresented cheques Rs 7,500 plus deposits in transit Rs 2,000 also gives Rs 92,100, so they match.','Reconcile a month of bank entries.','Difference after adjustments is zero.','Why do cash book and bank balance differ?','Timing items, charges and sometimes errors.'),
 M('Profit and loss and balance sheet','Create',6,['List income, then cost of goods sold, then expenses to reach net profit.','Adjust for closing stock, prepaid and accrued expenses and depreciation.','List assets and liabilities in order of liquidity on the balance sheet.','Check that assets equal liabilities plus equity including profit.'],'Sales Rs 6,40,000 less cost of goods Rs 4,10,000 gives gross profit Rs 2,30,000. Expenses Rs 1,45,000 leave net profit Rs 85,000, which is added to equity.','Produce statements for the month.','Net profit flows to equity and the balance sheet balances.','What is gross profit?','Sales minus the cost of goods sold.'),
 M('Tax, payroll and controls','Evaluate',6,['Calculate tax collected on sales less tax paid on purchases to find the payable amount.','Deduct tax at source from payments where the law requires and pay it by the due date.','Set controls: two people for cash, approvals for payments, monthly reconciliation.','Keep a calendar of filing dates and avoid late fees.'],'Output tax Rs 54,000, input tax Rs 38,500, so Rs 15,500 is payable by the due date. A late fee for each day of delay is avoided by filing on time (check the current fee and due dates with the tax authority).','Prepare a tax computation and a filing calendar.','Computation agrees with the books and the calendar lists each due date.','What is a control?','A step that prevents or catches errors and fraud.'),
 M('Capstone: a month of books','Create',5,['Record all transactions of the month from documents.','Reconcile the bank and count the cash.','Produce the trial balance and statements.','Present findings, errors found and fixes to a mentor.'],'A small shop with 120 transactions, sales Rs 6,40,000 and net profit Rs 85,000, with a reconciled bank.','Present the month pack.','Entries balance, bank ties out and statements agree.','What shows the books are reliable?','Documents, balanced entries and a reconciled bank.')],
 extra=[('Why keep cash and bank separate?','Each has its own balance that must be reconciled.'),('What is depreciation?','Spreading the cost of an asset over its useful life.')],
 rubric=RUB('Accuracy','Entries balance and statements agree','Controls','Reconciled monthly with approvals'),
 ladder=LAD('Know the accounting equation.','Record entries from documents.','Keep books for a small shop.','Prepare statements and tax computations.','Lead accounts for a growing business.','Design accounting systems and train teams.','Set standards for small business accounting and audit.'),
 jobs=['Bookkeeper','Accounts assistant','Accounts executive','Payroll clerk','Tax assistant']),

dict(slug='food-processing', title='Food Processing and Agri-Tech', level='L4 Practitioner',
 summary='Take produce from harvest to a safe packed product with good hygiene, correct preservation, measured critical points, cold chain, accurate labels and a plan for a small processing unit.',
 outs=[('Define','food hazards and hygiene rules.'),('Apply','preservation, heat treatment and packing steps.'),('Analyse','yield, losses and cost per kilogram.'),('Evaluate','a batch against a food-safety plan.'),('Create','a labelled product and a small unit plan.')],
 task='Produce a safe batch of a processed food such as mango pickle or fruit jam, keep a batch record, and write a small unit plan.', cond='About 12 weeks part-time. A clean kitchen or training unit, weighing scale, thermometer, pH strips or meter, clean jars, a mentor.',
 standard='Hygiene rules are followed, critical limits are measured and recorded for the batch, losses are calculated, and the label shows all required details correctly.', who='Farmers, food entrepreneurs, self-help group members, diploma students.', req='None.',
 mods=[
 M('Hygiene and food hazards','Define',4,['Name the hazards: biological such as germs, chemical such as cleaning liquid, physical such as hair or glass.','Wash hands with soap for 20 seconds before work and after the toilet, touching the face, or handling raw produce.','Cover hair, wear clean clothes, and cover cuts with a waterproof bandage and glove.','Use safe water, keep pests out and store waste in covered bins away from food.'],'A worker has a cut finger. It is covered with a blue bandage and a glove, and the worker is moved off raw handling. Water is tested and chlorinated to 0.2 to 0.5 parts per million.','Write a hygiene code for a small unit.','Code covers people, place, water and pests with a check for each.','Name three hazard types.','Biological, chemical and physical.'),
 M('Select and prepare raw material','Apply',5,['Check produce for ripeness, damage, mould and pesticide waiting period.','Sort and grade by size and quality; remove spoilt pieces before washing.','Wash in running safe water, then peel or cut with clean tools.','Weigh before and after each step and record it.'],'100 kg of mangoes: 8 kg rejected at sorting, 22 kg lost to peel and stone. 70 kg of usable pulp remains, so usable yield is 70 percent.','Prepare 10 kg of raw produce and record weights at each step.','Weights are recorded at each step and yield is calculated.','Why weigh at every step?','To find where losses occur.'),
 M('Preservation by heat, drying and acid','Apply',6,['Cook jam to 104 degrees Celsius, or until it reaches 65 percent sugar by a refractometer or the set test.','Use salt, oil and acid in pickles to stop growth of germs, with pH below 4.6.','Dry fruit or vegetables on clean trays at 55 to 60 degrees until crisp and moisture is low.','Keep boiling hot water, steam and open flames away from children and wear heat gloves.'],'Jam from 5 kg pulp and 4 kg sugar is boiled to 104 degrees Celsius for 25 minutes. The final pH is 3.4, which is safe, and the hot fill temperature is 85 degrees.','Build one batch of jam or pickle and record time, temperature and pH.','Critical limits are met and recorded at the time.','Why measure pH in pickles?','Below 4.6 stops harmful germs from growing.'),
 M('Packing and sealing','Apply',5,['Wash jars and lids and sterilise them in boiling water for 10 minutes.','Fill hot, leave 1 cm headspace, wipe the rim and seal at once.','Cool and check lids; reject any that bulge or leak.','Use food-grade packing and keep it covered until use.'],'A batch of 40 jars of 250 g is filled at 85 degrees. Two leak at the lid and are removed, so 38 jars are passed.','Pack and seal one batch and inspect every jar.','All sealed jars pass and rejects are recorded.','Why leave headspace?','It allows expansion and helps a good seal.'),
 M('Storage and cold chain','Apply',5,['Store dry goods off the floor, away from walls, in a cool dry store with first in, first out.','Keep perishable items at 4 degrees Celsius or lower and frozen items at minus 18.','Check and log fridge temperature twice a day.','Transport in clean, covered vehicles with insulated boxes and ice packs.'],'A cold room log shows 3 degrees in the morning and 9 degrees in the evening after a power cut. The stock is held and checked, and a generator is planned.','Set up a storage log and a stock rotation system.','Logs are filled twice daily and oldest stock is used first.','What does first in, first out mean?','The oldest stock is used or sold first.'),
 M('Quality and food safety plan','Evaluate',6,['List each step and its hazard, and mark the critical ones such as cooking, cooling, sealing and metal detection.','Set a limit, a check, a record and a correction for each critical step.','Take a sample of each batch for taste, colour, pH and seal checks.','Write a recall plan: batch number, buyers and how to stop sales.'],'Critical step: cooking to 104 degrees. Limit: at least 104. Check: thermometer each batch. Correction: continue boiling. Record: batch sheet signed.','Write a safety plan for your product.','Every critical step has limit, check, record and correction.','What is a critical limit?','A value that must be met to keep food safe.'),
 M('Labelling, cost and yield','Analyse',5,['Print on every label the name, ingredients, net weight, batch number, date of making, best before date and the maker name and address.','Show the 14-digit FSSAI licence or registration number, the veg or non-veg mark, MRP inclusive of taxes, and nutrition and allergen details as the labelling rules require.','Work out yield as finished weight divided by raw weight.','Work out cost per jar from raw material, fuel, packing, labour and overhead.'],'Cost of 38 jars: produce Rs 3,800, sugar Rs 1,800, packing Rs 760, fuel Rs 400, labour Rs 1,200 total Rs 7,960. Cost per jar is Rs 209, sold at Rs 280 for a margin of Rs 71.','Design a label and calculate cost per jar.','Label has all details and the cost sheet adds up.','Why print a batch number?','So that a problem batch can be traced.'),
 M('Capstone: batch and unit plan','Create',6,['Produce one batch with hygiene checks and a batch record.','Calculate yield, losses and cost.','Write a unit plan: space layout, equipment, licences, staff and monthly sales target.','Present the batch, label and plan to a mentor.'],'A unit of 20 square metres making 100 jars a week with a start-up cost of Rs 1,20,000 and a monthly profit of Rs 12,000.','Present the batch pack and unit plan.','Records are complete and the plan covers licences and costs.','What proves the batch was safe?','The record of measured critical limits and passed checks.')],
 extra=[('Why not reuse old jars without washing?','Residues can carry germs that spoil food or cause illness.'),('What is shelf life?','The time a food stays safe and good in stated storage conditions.')],
 rubric=RUB('Food safety','Critical limits measured and corrected','Product quality','Consistent across batches with checks'),
 ladder=LAD('Know hygiene rules and hazards.','Prepare and preserve a small batch safely.','Run batches with records and labels.','Operate a licensed small unit.','Manage production, quality and a team.','Lead a processing business with traceability.','Set standards for food processing and agri-tech training.'),
 jobs=['Food processing operator','Quality checker','Production supervisor','Food entrepreneur','Cold chain assistant']),
]
